{
  "@context": "https://doi.org/10.5063/schema/codemeta-2.0",
  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "sheepdog",
  "description": "Checks whether automated detections from 'BirdNET' custom classifiers in passive acoustic monitoring are real. Builds clip sets for manual validation (top-score, random-occasion or random-recording designs), following the multiple-method and observation-confirmation designs for false-positive occupancy models of Miller et al. (2011) <doi:10.1890/10-1396.1> and Chambert et al. (2015) <doi:10.1890/14-1507.1>, summarises the reviewed clips, converts confidence scores into probabilities of true detection, as described by Wood and Kahl (2024) <doi:10.1007/s10336-024-02144-5>, with hierarchical logistic models, and turns calibrated detections into nightly detection histories and effort-standardised community matrices.",
  "name": "sheepdog: Sample, Validate and Calibrate 'BirdNET' Detections",
  "relatedLink": "https://provetelab.org/sheepdog/",
